 "desc": "Goal: Learn ARM data processing instructions. ARM uses a 3-operand format: ADD Rd, Rn, Op2 means Rd = Rn + Op2. The barrel shifter lets you shift or rotate the second operand for free: MOV R5, R1, LSL #2 shifts R1 left by 2 before storing (equivalent to multiplying by 4). This is unique to ARM and extremely powerful.",
 "source": [
  "// ARM Data Processing",
  "// Format: OP Rd, Rn, Operand2",
  "// Barrel shifter: LSL, LSR, ASR, ROR",
  "",
  "mov r1, #7",
  "mov r2, #3",
  "add r0, r1, r2      ; r0 = 7 + 3",
  "sub r3, r0, #5      ; r3 = r0 - 5",
  "mul r4, r1, r0      ; r4 = r1 * r0",
  "mov r5, r1, LSL #2  ; r5 = r1 << 2 (r1 * 4)",
  "and r6, r0, r2      ; r6 = r0 AND r2",
  "orr r7, r1, r2      ; r7 = r1 OR r2",
  "hlt"
 ],
